{"user": "What's a stable edge?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:29:12.540974+00:00", "assistant": "A **stable edge** is a row/column of discs on the edge that **can\u2019t be flipped anymore**, usually because it is connected to a **corner**.\n\nExample: if White owns **a1** and the top edge has White discs next to it, those discs are very safe because nothing can outflank them from above.\n\nOn this board, White\u2019s **top edge** and **left edge** are stable, because White has the corners **a1, h1, a8** and solid edge lines. That gave White a big permanent disc advantage.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:29:12.540974+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:29:17.540974+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "do the pieces just stay there once they are in the corners?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:29:27.540974+00:00", "assistant": "Yes. **Once a disc is in a corner, it can never be flipped**.\n\nWhy: to flip a disc, it must be trapped between two opponent discs in a straight line. A corner has no square \u201cbehind\u201d it, so it can\u2019t be surrounded that way.\n\nThat\u2019s why corners are so powerful: they often make nearby edge discs stable too.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:29:27.540974+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:29:32.540974+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 2, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.6666666666666666, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction", "Positive Feedback"]}}
